. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3
. 
.         * The pre-analysis plan (PAP) initially proposed using an index of be
> haviors as the dependent variable. This index was to include three components
> : who in the household has the final say in financial decisions (plc0011), th
> e average working hours of each partner (lm0621), and the weekly time each pa
> rtner devotes to housework (pli0043_h). However, due to the very limited or n
> o overlap in the availability of data for lm0621, plc0011, and pli0043_h, con
> structing a reliable index was not feasible. As a result, we revised our appr
> oach and now use the weekly time devoted to housework (pli0043_v3) as the sol
> e behavioral indicator of gender equality within the household. Specifically,
>  we measure the absolute difference in housework hours between partners, with
>  larger values indicating greater inequality in the division of domestic labo
> r.
.         
.         * To test H3, we model the absolute difference in housework hours (ab
> s_pli0043_v3) as a function of whether the household includes a daughter (d_d
> aughter). The model controls for household-level fixed effects (i.hid) and ye
> ar fixed effects (i.syear).
.         
.         gen abs_pli0043_v3 = abs(pli0043_v3_1 - pli0043_v3_2)
(853 missing values generated)

.         label variable abs_pli0043_v3 "Absolute value of the difference betwe
> en partners for pli0043_v3"

. 
.         reg abs_pli0043_v3 d_daughter i.syear i.hid if sample == 1

